<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Palatine of Saxony</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The County Palatine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> was a medieval palatinate within the stem duchy of Saxony, whose counts palatine represented royal authority in the region around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unstrut">Unstrut</a>. It was held by the counts of Goseck and then of Sommerschenburg, and in 1180 passed to the Ludowingian landgraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>. After their extinction in 1247 it went with Thuringia to the Wettin dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-palatine-of-saxony.jpg" alt="County Palatine of Saxony" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Holy Roman Empereor of Habsburg and the Wettin House of Saxony · CC BY-SA 2.0 fr · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Augustus_III_of_Poland_as_vicar_of_the_Holy_Roman_Empire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
